<PageTitle>Pivot tables — FlexCore Showcase</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Pivot tables" Category="Data Grid" CategoryHref="demo/grid" ControlName="PivotControl"
                   Tagline="Cross-tabs with grouped headers, subtotals, several measures, sorting and a drag-and-drop field builder."
                   SourcePath="Grid/PivotControl.razor;Grid/PivotControl.razor.cs;Grid/PivotSortDescriptor.cs;Grid/GridEnums.cs;Grid/GridColumn.cs;Grid/GridControl.razor.cs">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            <code>PivotControl</code> turns a list of objects into a cross-tab: the values of the <code>RowFields</code> label the rows,
            the values of the <code>ColumnFields</code> spread across the columns, and each cell aggregates one or more measures with
            <code>Sum</code>, <code>Average</code>, <code>Count</code>, <code>Min</code> or <code>Max</code>. Two row fields give grouped rows
            with a subtotal per group; two column fields give a two-row header; more than one measure adds a sub-column per measure. Headers
            sort either a dimension or the rows by a column's values, and the sort keys can be read and set from the page. With
            <code>Interactive</code> the control adds the field builder: available fields, four drop zones and a filter bar.
        </p>
        <p>
            <code>GridControl</code> can switch into this control: <code>AllowPivoting</code> enables its embedded pivot view,
            <code>ShowPivotPanelButton</code> puts the button on the grid's option rail, and the grid's export then takes the pivot's rows and columns.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="builder" Title="Interactive builder" RazorCode="@Code.Builder" CSharpCode="@Code.BuilderCs">
            <Description><p>Drag a field from the list into Filters, Rows, Columns or Values; drag a chip to another area to move it; the ✕ removes it. Each value chip has an aggregation dropdown and a format box (a .NET numeric format such as N0 or C2; blank prints the plain number). A filter field adds a dropdown above the table that narrows the data before grouping. The arrows on row and column chips sort that dimension; a click on a column header sorts the rows by that column's values, and Shift-click adds a second key. The builder starts from the parameters below and then keeps its own state.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <PivotControl TValue="SaleRecord"
                              DataSource="@_sales"
                              RowFields="@_byCountry"
                              ColumnFields="@_byQuarterAndCategory"
                              ValueField="Amount"
                              ValueFormat="C0"
                              Interactive="true"
                              FieldLabels="@_labels"
                              Height="420px" />
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="grouped" Title="Grouped rows, subtotals and two measures" RazorCode="@Code.Grouped" CSharpCode="@Code.GroupedCs">
            <Description><p>Two row fields: Country spans its categories and a "Country Total" row closes each group. Two measures: Revenue and Units sit side by side under each quarter and under Total, each with its own format and label. Click a header to sort by that column (ascending, then descending, then off); Shift-click adds a key; rows stay inside their country when sorted by a value. The buttons set <code>SortDescriptors</code> from the page, and the line below shows the keys the control reports through <code>SortDescriptorsChanged</code>, whichever side changed them.</p></Description>
            <Controls>
                <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="@(() => _sorts = [new("Country", SortDirection.Descending)])">Countries Z to A</ButtonControl>
                <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="@(() => _sorts = [])">Clear sort</ButtonControl>
            </Controls>
            <Demo>
                <PivotControl TValue="SaleRecord"
                              DataSource="@_sales"
                              RowFields="@_byCountryAndCategory"
                              ColumnFields="@_byQuarter"
                              ValueFields="@_measures"
                              SortDescriptors="@_sorts"
                              SortDescriptorsChanged="s => _sorts = s"
                              Height="480px" />
                <p class="result">Sort: @SortText</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="formulas" Title="Formula columns in a grid" RazorCode="@Code.Formulas" CSharpCode="@Code.FormulasCs">
            <Description><p>Not a pivot, but the other way to compute numbers in a table. A column's <code>Formula</code> is evaluated per row: <code>[Field]</code> references and bare property names are replaced by the row's values and the expression runs through .NET's <code>DataTable.Compute</code>, so arithmetic, comparisons, <code>IIF</code> and the other DataColumn expression functions work. With <code>AllowCellFormulas</code>, a text cell that starts with <code>=</code> is evaluated the same way; the Commission column reads a property that returns <code>=[Revenue] * 0.08</code>. Values that are not numbers count as 0, and an expression that fails shows as <code>#</code> followed by the expression. The results are display only; the row's data is not changed.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <GridControl TValue="Deal" DataSource="@_deals"
                             AllowCellFormulas="true"
                             AllowSorting="true"
                             AllowFiltering="true"
                             AllowResizing="true"
                             Height="360px">
                    <GridColumnsBase>
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(Deal.Region)" HeaderText="Region" Width="120px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(Deal.Rep)" HeaderText="Rep" Width="140px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(Deal.Product)" HeaderText="Product" Width="120px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(Deal.Revenue)" HeaderText="Revenue" Type="ColumnType.Number" Format="C0" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" Width="120px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(Deal.Cost)" HeaderText="Cost" Type="ColumnType.Number" Format="C0" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" Width="120px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="GrossMargin" HeaderText="Gross margin" Formula="[Revenue] - [Cost]" Type="ColumnType.Number" Format="C0" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" Width="140px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="MarginPct" HeaderText="Margin %" Formula="([Revenue] - [Cost]) / [Revenue]" Type="ColumnType.Number" Format="P1" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" Width="120px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(Deal.CommissionFormula)" HeaderText="Commission" Type="ColumnType.Number" Format="C0" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" Width="130px" />
                    </GridColumnsBase>
                </GridControl>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

    <Vocabulary>
        <DocSections>
            <DocSection Id="doc-pivotcontrol-tvalue-parameters" Title="PivotControl&lt;TValue&gt; parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Params.Length, "parameters")' Open="true">
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="PivotControl&lt;TValue&gt; parameters" Rows="Vocab.Params" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-pivotcontrol-events" Title="PivotControl events" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Events.Length, "events")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Events" Title="PivotControl events" Rows="Vocab.Events" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-pivotcontrol-methods" Title="PivotControl methods" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Methods.Length, "methods")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Methods" Title="PivotControl methods" Rows="Vocab.Methods" />
                <p>
                <code>PivotSortDescriptor(string Field, SortDirection Direction)</code> is a record: <code>Field</code> is a row field, a column
                field or the generated name of a value column, which the control writes into each header's <code>data-sort-field</code> attribute.
                <code>AggregateType</code> is <code>Sum</code>, <code>Average</code>, <code>Count</code>, <code>Min</code> or <code>Max</code>.
                </p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-pivotvalueconfig" Title="PivotValueConfig" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Measure.Length, "properties")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="PivotValueConfig" Rows="Vocab.Measure" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-formula-cells-on-gridcontrol" Title="Formula cells on GridControl" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Formula.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="Formula cells on GridControl" Rows="Vocab.Formula" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-css-classes" Title="CSS classes" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Css.Length, "classes")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssClasses" Title="CSS classes" Rows="Vocab.Css" />
            </DocSection>
        </DocSections>
    </Vocabulary>

    <Accessibility>
        <p>
            Sortable headers are buttons titled "Sort <em>header</em>" and carry <code>aria-sort</code> while sorted; the chips' sort arrows
            are buttons too. The filter dropdowns are native selects with a visible label. The builder's chips move by mouse drag only:
            apart from each chip's remove button and the aggregation and format controls, there is no keyboard way to place a field.
        </p>
    </Accessibility>

    <Related>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="demo/grid/grouping">Grouping &amp; totals</a>: the same aggregates as group captions and footers inside a grid.</li>
            <li><a href="demo/grid">Grid overview</a>: the grid that can switch into the embedded pivot view.</li>
        </ul>
    </Related>
</FeatureDemoLayout>

